 | Native inline finalization, including a canonical semantic no-op | Route the exact native-owned field's actual final DOM/cache completion directly through the same BlockReconciler owner before synchronization returns. Canonical equality may suppress the engine transaction, but must not suppress real completion. No transaction event or afterNativeEdit observer is used as its delivery prerequisite. |
 | Removal, destruction, failure without completion or supersession | No completion of the old occurrence. Same-ID successors and a later cached-field return cannot revive a retired callback's authority. Ordinary uncommitted DOM changes alone do not authorize notification. |
 
